Exercise 2.2 — Calibration probe (mirrors Paper 1's method)

Q1: "What percentage of breast cancers are HER2-positive? Answer with a number and a confidence score from 0-
100%."

Q2 (reworded): "Roughly what fraction of breast cancer diagnoses show HER2 positivity? Give a number and how
confident you are (0-100%)."

Ask both questions to the same model. If the numeric answer or stated confidence shifts noticeably between the two
phrasings, you've just reproduced Paper 1's core finding on structural inconsistency — firsthand.

